<article class="env-lemma" id="0EBA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EBA">Lemma <span data-tag="0EBA">15.24.16</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian domain. Let $M$ be a finite reflexive $R$-module. Let $\mathfrak p \subset R$ be a prime ideal. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $\text{depth}(R_\mathfrak p) \geq 2$, then $\text{depth}(M_\mathfrak p) \geq 2$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $R$ is $(S_2)$, then $M$ is $(S_2)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since formation of reflexive hull $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, R), R)$ commutes with localization (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0583" data-tag="0583">10.10.2</a>) part (1) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AV5" data-tag="0AV5">15.24.10</a>. Part (2) is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AV6" data-tag="0AV6">15.24.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>